    think:{quote:"After his talk with Mr. Spencer, Holden sits alone in his dormitory, thinking about how easily people, and schools, seem to give up on each other.", question:"Why might Holden feel both nervous and lonely as he prepares to leave Pencey Prep?", options:["Because he is excited about a new adventure","Because leaving another school reminds him how easily things end badly for him","Because he dislikes his family"], answer:1, note:"Being expelled again makes Holden doubt himself, even though he tries hard to seem unbothered by it."},
