    think:{quote:"At the museum, standing in front of the same still, silent glass cases from his childhood, Holden feels briefly safe, as if nothing about him had changed either.", question:"Why does Holden find comfort in a museum where nothing ever changes?", options:["Because he dislikes learning new things","Because his own life feels confusing, so unchanging places feel safe","Because Phoebe asked him to visit it"], answer:1, note:"Holden struggles with change and loss, so places that stay exactly the same offer him a rare, simple kind of comfort."},
