    think:{quote:"When Phoebe asks him to name one thing he truly likes, Holden can only describe a strange daydream: standing in a big field of rye, catching children before they run off the edge of a cliff.", question:"What might Holden's daydream about catching children reveal about him?", options:["That he wants a job outdoors","That he wants to protect other people's innocence, even though he cannot protect his own","That he is planning to become a teacher"], answer:1, note:"This daydream shows how much Holden wants to stop others losing the safety and innocence that he feels he has already lost."},
